{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HVNnFeoWcF3sr6KSujLoJz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor Calendar v1 â€” MASTER PLAN\n2\t\n3\t**Stage:** Crucible Stage 1 (Master Plan) Â· **Date:** 2026-06-20 Â· **Depth:** FULL\n4\t**Status:** DRAFT â€” awaiting John's Stage-1 approval (then â†’ Stage 2 Implementation Plan)\n5\t**Research base:** `planning/calendar-research/run-2026-06-20/CONSOLIDATED-BRIEF.md` (vetted, merges run-2026-06-15 + run-2026-06-17)\n6\t**Build vehicle:** the trio â€” Foreman builds wave-by-wave; every wave fully-stubbed-healthchecked (never live Google/MS) + UI sign-off per the v2â€“v11 standard.\n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## 1. North Star (LOCKED 2026-06-20)\n11\t\n12\t> **Anchor displays all of John's Google + Outlook/M365 calendars in a real calendar view, and pushes John's Anchor-owned events out to a dedicated Anchor-owned calendar in each provider â€” fully local and private (no cloud, no inbound/public network surface) â€” and it can NEVER corrupt, delete, or duplicate a human-created event in John's real calendars.**\n13\t\n14\t**Falsifiers (any one fails the objective):**\n15\t- (a) any write path that can mutate a non-Anchor-owned event;\n16\t- (b) any inbound/public network surface or webhook dependency;\n17\t- (c) a sync bug that silently loses or duplicates events;\n18\t- (d) a calendar dependency that breaks `distro.py`'s stdlib-only scan *outside* the declared `[calendar]` extra;\n19\t- (e) a render path that makes a synchronous network call.\n20\t\n21\tEvery wave below must serve this North Star (the inclusion test). Anything that doesn't is cut or Grass-caught.\n22\t\n23\t---\n24\t\n25\t## 2. LOCKED architecture (from research; do not re-litigate)\n26\t\n27\t- **Poll, don't webhook.** Background `threading.Thread(daemon=True)` poll (mirror `anchor_gui._trigger_session_summary`). Render reads cached `.anchor/calendar/state.json` ONLY â€” never a sync network call (falsifier e). Cadence 5â€“15 min foreground / hourly background.\n28\t- **Two native REST clients:** Google Calendar v3 (`events.list` + `syncToken`; `410`â†’full resync) + Microsoft Graph (`GET /me/calendarView/delta` â€” GA v1.0, NOT beta `/events/delta`; `@odata.deltaLink`; guard the `skipToken` infinite loop). Pull recurring series un-expanded (`singleEvents=false`).\n29\t- **Auth:** OAuth2 Auth-Code + PKCE (S256), installed/desktop client, loopback `http://127.0.0.1:<ephemeral>/callback` (never `localhost`, never 8777). `webbrowser.open()` consent. DPAPI user-scope token storage via `ctypes` (`CryptProtectData`) â€” service runs as `.\\john`. Document the user+machine-bound DPAPI footgun.\n30\t\n31\t## 3. Resolved decisions (locked for this plan)\n32\t\n33\t| # | Decision | Resolution |\n34\t|---|---|---|\n35\t| A | OAuth implementation | **`[calendar]` optional pip-extra** (`msal` + `google-auth`), lazy/degrade like `[terminal]=pywinpty`, in `distro.py`'s scoped allowlist. Still DPAPI-wrap at rest. |\n36\t| B | Sync scope | **TWO one-way pipes** (push Anchor-owned â†’ dedicated Anchor calendar; pull all others read-only). NO symmetric three-way merge. Symmetric merge DEFERRED behind the dual-writer tripwire (Â§8). |\n37\t| C1 | Recurrence expander | **(a) Accept `allenporter/ical` inside the `[calendar]` extra + distro allowlist** (John, 2026-06-20). Adds a compiled native wheel (pydantic) but only in the opt-in extra; avoids hand-rolling the silent-failure-prone recurrence engine. |\n38\t| C2 | Google OAuth posture | **Design for Production** (durable refresh for unattended sync); **build the token store to tolerate 7-day expiry** as a fallback; the 8-day durable-refresh spike confirms before write-back ships (John, 2026-06-20). |\n39\t\n40\t## 4. Component picks (folded in)\n41\t\n42\t- **UI:** vendored **EventCalendar (vkurko, MIT)** in `vendor/event-calendar/` â€” **ship its LICENSE file** (no `license` field in package.json); FullCalendar **v6** is the named fallback (NOT v7 â€” adds a temporal-polyfill peer dep). Widget renders **pre-expanded** occurrences â†’ the backend owns 100% of recurrence correctness.\n43\t- **Event store:** RFC-5545 **`.ics`-per-series + `meta.json` sidecar** under `.anchor/calendar/<account>/events/<icalUID>.ics`. **Sidecar MUST retain raw Graph JSON** (Graph `relativeMonthly`/`relativeYearly` with multiple `daysOfWeek` has no clean RRULE form â€” lossy). Override identity keyed `(iCalUID, original-start)`.\n44\t- **Sync engine:** hand-rolled two pipes; reference vdirsyncer's BSD `sync.py` â€” **copy its empty-replica \"a replica went empty â‡’ abort, don't propagate deletes\" guard** (cheap insurance against falsifier c).\n45\t\n46\t---\n47\t\n48\t## 5. Assumption map â†’ premortem â†’ mitigations\n49\t\n50\t**Load-bearing assumptions:** (1) a Production-unverified Google app holds a durable refresh token for the sensitive scope â€” *UNVERIFIED, spike-gated*; (2) `ical`'s Timeline covers John's real RRULE surface â€” *spike-gated*; (3) Graph `recurrencePattern`â†’RRULE is lossy only in the enumerated relative-monthly/yearly cells â€” *spike-gated*; (4) the DPAPI/PKCE/loopback infra works â€” *OBSERVED, spike done*.\n51\t\n52\t**Premortem â€” how v1 dies, and the mitigation baked into the plan:**\n53\t\n54\t| Death | Mitigation (now a plan requirement) |\n55\t|---|---|\n56\t| **Echo display** â€” the PULL pipe reads ALL calendars *including Anchor's own dedicated calendar*, so pushed events render twice / fight the local copy *(Shark finding #1, BLOCKER)* | The pull pipe **excludes the Anchor-owned calendar id** from inbound display; Anchor's own events render from local `state.json`, never from a pull of its own calendar. Explicit wave acceptance criterion. |\n57\t| **Silent sync death** â€” the 7-day token expires (C2) or `invalid_grant` hits mid-background-poll; sync just stops; user thinks the calendar is current *(falsifier c-adjacent; Shark finding #3)* | The daemon detects `invalid_grant`/token-loss and surfaces an explicit **\"Calendar needs re-auth\"** state on the dashboard â€” **never a silent stop**. A poll-failure timestamp is visible. |\n58\t| **Recurring-event corruption on write** | Structurally prevented by the safety rail (write only to the Anchor-owned calendar) + override identity `(iCalUID, original-start)` + never rewrite a series `DTSTART`. |\n59\t| **Distro scan breaks** (falsifier d) | `ical`+pydantic live ONLY in the `[calendar]` extra + `distro.py` allowlist; Wave 1 adds a healthcheck assertion that the core import path stays stdlib-clean without the extra. |\n60\t| **The recurrence spike reveals a huge lossy-cell count** late | The Graph-recurrence enumeration spike is a **gate BEFORE the recurrence-hardening wave is estimated** (Â§7), not a discovery mid-build. |\n61\t\n62\t---\n63\t\n64\t## 6. Phased structure (master-plan altitude; Stage 2 decomposes to waves w/ acceptance criteria)\n65\t\n66\tThe dependency order is forced: store â†’ auth â†’ pull+display â†’ push â†’ harden â†’ ship.\n67\t\n68\t1. **Phase 1 â€” Event store + `[calendar]` extra foundation.** ICS-per-series + sidecar; `paths.calendar_dir()`; markdown-deadlineâ†’store mapping; declare the `[calendar]` extra (`msal`, `google-auth`, `icalendar`, `allenporter/ical`) + `distro.py` allowlist + the stdlib-clean-without-extra assertion. *Near-zero blast radius.*\n69\t2. **Phase 2 â€” Auth.** PKCE + loopback + DPAPI, thin wrappers over `msal`/`google-auth`. Reuse the OBSERVED 2026-06-15 spike harness. Production-posture config; token store tolerant of 7-day expiry; `invalid_grant`â†’re-auth surfaced state.\n70\t3. **Phase 3 â€” PULL pipe + EventCalendar display.** Both providers, incremental (syncToken/delta), `410`/token-lossâ†’full resync, empty-replica abort guard. Expand recurrence via `ical` Timeline â†’ render month/week/day. **Excludes the Anchor-owned calendar from inbound.** Render reads cache only.\n71\t4. **Phase 4 â€” PUSH pipe** to the dedicated Anchor-owned calendar (create-if-absent). Upsert by `iCalUID`; echo-suppress (self-marker + recorded ETag); Graph `transactionId` idempotent create. **Gated on the 8-day durable-refresh spike.**\n72\t5. **Phase 5 â€” Recurrence hardening.** The Graph `recurrencePattern` fixture table; sidecar-only fallback for lossy cells; override-identity correctness tests.\n73\t6. **Phase 6 â€” Ship.** CLI read-mirror (`cal status`/`cal pull`); fully-stubbed `check_calendar_surface` healthcheck (never live Google/MS); distro scan green; CLAUDE.md. *(PROJECT DONE.)*\n74\t\n75\t---\n76\t\n77\t## 7. Spikes & gates\n78\t\n79\t- **Graph-recurrence enumeration spike (1 day, no accounts needed)** â€” enumerate every `recurrencePattern` variant into a clean-RRULE-vs-sidecar-only fixture table. **Gates the Phase-5 estimate.** Can run now / in parallel with Stage 2.\n80\t- **8-day durable-refresh spike** (needs John's Google app registration + consent + wall-clock) â€” confirms the Production-unverified durable-RT assumption. **Gates Phase 4 (write-back) only**, not planning. Runbook: `run-2026-06-15/spike/RUNBOOK.md`.\n81\t- **MSA vs work/school** â€” confirm which Microsoft account John connects (changes `/common` vs `/consumers` + RT reliability) before Phase 2 locks the authority.\n82\t\n83\t## 8. Out of scope (v1) + the tripwire\n84\t\n85\t- **Symmetric two-way merge** over dual-writer events â€” DEFERRED. **Tripwire:** returns ONLY when a user is allowed to natively edit/delete, *inside Anchor*, an event an external provider also mutates. Until then two one-way pipes are correct and sufficient.\n86\t- **Editing the user's PRIMARY calendars from Anchor** â€” explicitly out; a later opt-in.\n87\t- No SaaS aggregator (Nylas/Cronofy/Cal.com) â€” all require cloud + public webhook (falsifier b).\n88\t\n89\t## 9. Verification standard (non-negotiable)\n90\t\n91\tEvery wave: a **fully-stubbed** healthcheck slice (fake HTTP responder seam; never live Google/MS). Every UI wave: DOM assertions + Playwright + Chromium interaction test + screenshot + John's sign-off (the v4 lesson). `distro.py` import scan stays green (only the declared `pywinpty` + the new scoped `[calendar]` allowlist). Playwright stays DEV-ONLY (`pytest.importorskip`), never in product code.\n92\t\n93\t---\n94\t\n95\t## 10. Shark-Tank record (Stage 1, FULL)\n96\t\n97\t3 fresh-context Sharks (Skeptic / Contrarian / Analyst), each prompted to refute, North Star embedded. BLOCKER = â‰¥2 agree.\n98\t\n99\t- **Finding #1 (Skeptic + Analyst agree â†’ BLOCKER):** the pull pipe re-ingesting Anchor's own dedicated calendar causes echo/double-render. â†’ **Resolved:** Â§5 + Phase 3 exclude-own-calendar acceptance criterion.\n100\t- **Finding #2 (Contrarian):** \"the richer ICS store was justified as the *merge* prerequisite, which is now deferred â€” is it still needed?\" â†’ **Resolved (kept, re-justified):** markdown cannot hold RRULE/EXDATE/VTIMEZONE; faithful recurring **display** + the push source both require it. It earns its place under the new scope; it is no longer safety-gating. Not bloat (passes the inclusion test).\n101\t- **Finding #3 (Analyst):** silent sync death on the 7-day/`invalid_grant` path. â†’ **Resolved:** Â§5 explicit \"needs re-auth\" surfaced state â€” no silent stop.\n102\t- **Convergence:** a second round produced no new AXIS finding (dry). Stage 1 converged.\n103\t\n104\t---\n105\t\n106\t**Next:** on John's approval â†’ **Stage 2 Implementation Plan** (decompose Phases 1â€“6 into Foreman waves with per-wave `done-when` + Given/When/Then acceptance criteria), Shark-Tank to convergence, well-formedness gate (`locate-plan.mjs`), then the Foreman handoff doc-trio + `foreman.config.json`.\n107\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e78d70e-5840-44b3-bad2-ee6581f68d36","uuid":"ffe97312-3525-4ee3-81f5-a9f6254513ff","timestamp":"2026-06-21T04:59:59.983Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Anchor\\planning\\calendar-v1\\MASTER-PLAN.md","content":"# Anchor Calendar v1 â€” MASTER PLAN\n\n**Stage:** Crucible Stage 1 (Master Plan) Â· **Date:** 2026-06-20 Â· **Depth:** FULL\n**Status:** DRAFT â€” awaiting John's Stage-1 approval (then â†’ Stage 2 Implementation Plan)\n**Research base:** `planning/calendar-research/run-2026-06-20/CONSOLIDATED-BRIEF.md` (vetted, merges run-2026-06-15 + run-2026-06-17)\n**Build vehicle:** the trio â€” Foreman builds wave-by-wave; every wave fully-stubbed-healthchecked (never live Google/MS) + UI sign-off per the v2â€“v11 standard.\n\n---\n\n## 1. North Star (LOCKED 2026-06-20)\n\n> **Anchor displays all of John's Google + Outlook/M365 calendars in a real calendar view, and pushes John's Anchor-owned events out to a dedicated Anchor-owned calendar in each provider â€” fully local and private (no cloud, no inbound/public network surface) â€” and it can NEVER corrupt, delete, or duplicate a human-created event in John's real calendars.**\n\n**Falsifiers (any one fails the objective):**\n- (a) any write path that can mutate a non-Anchor-owned event;\n- (b) any inbound/public network surface or webhook dependency;\n- (c) a sync bug that silently loses or duplicates events;\n- (d) a calendar dependency that breaks `distro.py`'s stdlib-only scan *outside* the declared `[calendar]` extra;\n- (e) a render path that makes a synchronous network call.\n\nEvery wave below must serve this North Star (the inclusion test). Anything that doesn't is cut or Grass-caught.\n\n---\n\n## 2. LOCKED architecture (from research; do not re-litigate)\n\n- **Poll, don't webhook.** Background `threading.Thread(daemon=True)` poll (mirror `anchor_gui._trigger_session_summary`). Render reads cached `.anchor/calendar/state.json` ONLY â€” never a sync network call (falsifier e). Cadence 5â€“15 min foreground / hourly background.\n- **Two native REST clients:** Google Calendar v3 (`events.list` + `syncToken`; `410`â†’full resync) + Microsoft Graph (`GET /me/calendarView/delta` â€” GA v1.0, NOT beta `/events/delta`; `@odata.deltaLink`; guard the `skipToken` infinite loop). Pull recurring series un-expanded (`singleEvents=false`).\n- **Auth:** OAuth2 Auth-Code + PKCE (S256), installed/desktop client, loopback `http://127.0.0.1:<ephemeral>/callback` (never `localhost`, never 8777). `webbrowser.open()` consent. DPAPI user-scope token storage via `ctypes` (`CryptProtectData`) â€” service runs as `.\\john`. Document the user+machine-bound DPAPI footgun.\n\n## 3. Resolved decisions (locked for this plan)\n\n| # | Decision | Resolution |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | OAuth implementation | **`[calendar]` optional pip-extra** (`msal` + `google-auth`), lazy/degrade like `[terminal]=pywinpty`, in `distro.py`'s scoped allowlist. Still DPAPI-wrap at rest. |\n| B | Sync scope | **TWO one-way pipes** (push Anchor-owned â†’ dedicated Anchor calendar; pull all others read-only). NO symmetric three-way merge. Symmetric merge DEFERRED behind the dual-writer tripwire (Â§8). |\n| C1 | Recurrence expander | **(a) Accept `allenporter/ical` inside the `[calendar]` extra + distro allowlist** (John, 2026-06-20). Adds a compiled native wheel (pydantic) but only in the opt-in extra; avoids hand-rolling the silent-failure-prone recurrence engine. |\n| C2 | Google OAuth posture | **Design for Production** (durable refresh for unattended sync); **build the token store to tolerate 7-day expiry** as a fallback; the 8-day durable-refresh spike confirms before write-back ships (John, 2026-06-20). |\n\n## 4. Component picks (folded in)\n\n- **UI:** vendored **EventCalendar (vkurko, MIT)** in `vendor/event-calendar/` â€” **ship its LICENSE file** (no `license` field in package.json); FullCalendar **v6** is the named fallback (NOT v7 â€” adds a temporal-polyfill peer dep). Widget renders **pre-expanded** occurrences â†’ the backend owns 100% of recurrence correctness.\n- **Event store:** RFC-5545 **`.ics`-per-series + `meta.json` sidecar** under `.anchor/calendar/<account>/events/<icalUID>.ics`. **Sidecar MUST retain raw Graph JSON** (Graph `relativeMonthly`/`relativeYearly` with multiple `daysOfWeek` has no clean RRULE form â€” lossy). Override identity keyed `(iCalUID, original-start)`.\n- **Sync engine:** hand-rolled two pipes; reference vdirsyncer's BSD `sync.py` â€” **copy its empty-replica \"a replica went empty â‡’ abort, don't propagate deletes\" guard** (cheap insurance against falsifier c).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Assumption map â†’ premortem â†’ mitigations\n\n**Load-bearing assumptions:** (1) a Production-unverified Google app holds a durable refresh token for the sensitive scope â€” *UNVERIFIED, spike-gated*; (2) `ical`'s Timeline covers John's real RRULE surface â€” *spike-gated*; (3) Graph `recurrencePattern`â†’RRULE is lossy only in the enumerated relative-monthly/yearly cells â€” *spike-gated*; (4) the DPAPI/PKCE/loopback infra works â€” *OBSERVED, spike done*.\n\n**Premortem â€” how v1 dies, and the mitigation baked into the plan:**\n\n| Death | Mitigation (now a plan requirement) |\n|---|---|\n| **Echo display** â€” the PULL pipe reads ALL calendars *including Anchor's own dedicated calendar*, so pushed events render twice / fight the local copy *(Shark finding #1, BLOCKER)* | The pull pipe **excludes the Anchor-owned calendar id** from inbound display; Anchor's own events render from local `state.json`, never from a pull of its own calendar. Explicit wave acceptance criterion. |\n| **Silent sync death** â€” the 7-day token expires (C2) or `invalid_grant` hits mid-background-poll; sync just stops; user thinks the calendar is current *(falsifier c-adjacent; Shark finding #3)* | The daemon detects `invalid_grant`/token-loss and surfaces an explicit **\"Calendar needs re-auth\"** state on the dashboard â€” **never a silent stop**. A poll-failure timestamp is visible. |\n| **Recurring-event corruption on write** | Structurally prevented by the safety rail (write only to the Anchor-owned calendar) + override identity `(iCalUID, original-start)` + never rewrite a series `DTSTART`. |\n| **Distro scan breaks** (falsifier d) | `ical`+pydantic live ONLY in the `[calendar]` extra + `distro.py` allowlist; Wave 1 adds a healthcheck assertion that the core import path stays stdlib-clean without the extra. |\n| **The recurrence spike reveals a huge lossy-cell count** late | The Graph-recurrence enumeration spike is a **gate BEFORE the recurrence-hardening wave is estimated** (Â§7), not a discovery mid-build. |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Phased structure (master-plan altitude; Stage 2 decomposes to waves w/ acceptance criteria)\n\nThe dependency order is forced: store â†’ auth â†’ pull+display â†’ push â†’ harden â†’ ship.\n\n1. **Phase 1 â€” Event store + `[calendar]` extra foundation.** ICS-per-series + sidecar; `paths.calendar_dir()`; markdown-deadlineâ†’store mapping; declare the `[calendar]` extra (`msal`, `google-auth`, `icalendar`, `allenporter/ical`) + `distro.py` allowlist + the stdlib-clean-without-extra assertion. *Near-zero blast radius.*\n2. **Phase 2 â€” Auth.** PKCE + loopback + DPAPI, thin wrappers over `msal`/`google-auth`. Reuse the OBSERVED 2026-06-15 spike harness. Production-posture config; token store tolerant of 7-day expiry; `invalid_grant`â†’re-auth surfaced state.\n3. **Phase 3 â€” PULL pipe + EventCalendar display.** Both providers, incremental (syncToken/delta), `410`/token-lossâ†’full resync, empty-replica abort guard. Expand recurrence via `ical` Timeline â†’ render month/week/day. **Excludes the Anchor-owned calendar from inbound.** Render reads cache only.\n4. **Phase 4 â€” PUSH pipe** to the dedicated Anchor-owned calendar (create-if-absent). Upsert by `iCalUID`; echo-suppress (self-marker + recorded ETag); Graph `transactionId` idempotent create. **Gated on the 8-day durable-refresh spike.**\n5. **Phase 5 â€” Recurrence hardening.** The Graph `recurrencePattern` fixture table; sidecar-only fallback for lossy cells; override-identity correctness tests.\n6. **Phase 6 â€” Ship.** CLI read-mirror (`cal status`/`cal pull`); fully-stubbed `check_calendar_surface` healthcheck (never live Google/MS); distro scan green; CLAUDE.md. *(PROJECT DONE.)*\n\n---\n\n## 7. Spikes & gates\n\n- **Graph-recurrence enumeration spike (1 day, no accounts needed)** â€” enumerate every `recurrencePattern` variant into a clean-RRULE-vs-sidecar-only fixture table. **Gates the Phase-5 estimate.** Can run now / in parallel with Stage 2.\n- **8-day durable-refresh spike** (needs John's Google app registration + consent + wall-clock) â€” confirms the Production-unverified durable-RT assumption. **Gates Phase 4 (write-back) only**, not planning. Runbook: `run-2026-06-15/spike/RUNBOOK.md`.\n- **MSA vs work/school** â€” confirm which Microsoft account John connects (changes `/common` vs `/consumers` + RT reliability) before Phase 2 locks the authority.\n\n## 8. Out of scope (v1) + the tripwire\n\n- **Symmetric two-way merge** over dual-writer events â€” DEFERRED. **Tripwire:** returns ONLY when a user is allowed to natively edit/delete, *inside Anchor*, an event an external provider also mutates. Until then two one-way pipes are correct and sufficient.\n- **Editing the user's PRIMARY calendars from Anchor** â€” explicitly out; a later opt-in.\n- No SaaS aggregator (Nylas/Cronofy/Cal.com) â€” all require cloud + public webhook (falsifier b).\n\n## 9. Verification standard (non-negotiable)\n\nEvery wave: a **fully-stubbed** healthcheck slice (fake HTTP responder seam; never live Google/MS). Every UI wave: DOM assertions + Playwright + Chromium interaction test + screenshot + John's sign-off (the v4 lesson). `distro.py` import scan stays green (only the declared `pywinpty` + the new scoped `[calendar]` allowlist). Playwright stays DEV-ONLY (`pytest.importorskip`), never in product code.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Shark-Tank record (Stage 1, FULL)\n\n3 fresh-context Sharks (Skeptic / Contrarian / Analyst), each prompted to refute, North Star embedded. BLOCKER = â‰¥2 agree.\n\n- **Finding #1 (Skeptic + Analyst agree â†’ BLOCKER):** the pull pipe re-ingesting Anchor's own dedicated calendar causes echo/double-render. â†’ **Resolved:** Â§5 + Phase 3 exclude-own-calendar acceptance criterion.\n- **Finding #2 (Contrarian):** \"the richer ICS store was justified as the *merge* prerequisite, which is now deferred â€” is it still needed?\" â†’ **Resolved (kept, re-justified):** markdown cannot hold RRULE/EXDATE/VTIMEZONE; faithful recurring **display** + the push source both require it. It earns its place under the new scope; it is no longer safety-gating. Not bloat (passes the inclusion test).\n- **Finding #3 (Analyst):** silent sync death on the 7-day/`invalid_grant` path. â†’ **Resolved:** Â§5 explicit \"needs re-auth\" surfaced state â€” no silent stop.\n- **Convergence:** a second round produced no new AXIS finding (dry). Stage 1 converged.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** on John's approval â†’ **Stage 2 Implementation Plan** (decompose Phases 1â€“6 into Foreman waves with per-wave `done-when` + Given/When/Then acceptance criteria), Shark-Tank to convergence, well-formedness gate (`locate-plan.mjs`), then the Foreman handoff doc-trio + `foreman.config.json`.\n","numLines":107,"startLine":1,"totalLines":107}}}
