{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TQ1KpVNjW69zbo51ZQZhS5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor Calendar v1 â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n2\t\n3\t> Crucible Stage 2 output, locked 2026-06-20. Frozen design: `MASTER-PLAN.md`.\n4\t> Build cwd = repo root `C:\\dev\\Anchor`. Suggested branch: `foreman/calendar-v1` (off master).\n5\t> North Star + falsifiers are in `MASTER-PLAN.md Â§1` â€” every wave serves them.\n6\t\n7\ttest-command: python -m pytest -q\n8\t\n9\t## Conventions (read before any wave)\n10\t\n11\t- **No live Google / Microsoft, ever, in any test or healthcheck.** All HTTP goes through a\n12\t  fake-responder seam (monkeypatch the `urllib`/client transport â†’ `tests/fake_calendar_api.py`).\n13\t  No real OAuth dance, no real network, no real DPAPI key material in CI logic.\n14\t- **The `[calendar]` extra is opt-in + lazy + degrading.** `msal`, `google-auth`, `icalendar`,\n15\t  `allenporter/ical` (PyPI `ical`) are imported LAZILY inside the calendar modules only, exactly\n16\t  like `pywinpty` in `pty_manager.py`. With the extra absent, `import`-ing the calendar modules\n17\t  must succeed and surface a `CalendarUnavailable` (\"calendar unavailable\"), never a stack trace.\n18\t  `distro.py`'s import scan gets a NEW scoped allowlist entry for the calendar module(s) only;\n19\t  the core import path must stay stdlib-clean WITHOUT the extra (asserted in Wave 1).\n20\t- **Safety rail (falsifier a):** Anchor only ever issues create/update/delete against the\n21\t  dedicated Anchor-owned calendar it creates per provider. It NEVER holds a write/delete handle\n22\t  on any other calendar. Enforced in code (the push client refuses a non-Anchor calendar id) and\n23\t  tested negatively.\n24\t- **Render reads cache only (falsifier e):** the dashboard/calendar view reads\n25\t  `.anchor/calendar/state.json`; it never makes a sync network call on render.\n26\t- **Token storage:** DPAPI user-scope via `ctypes` `CryptProtectData` (service runs as `.\\john`).\n27\t  The token store tolerates 7-day expiry / `invalid_grant` by surfacing a re-auth state, never a\n28\t  silent stop (Shark finding #3).\n29\t- **UI verification (the v4 lesson)** for UI-changing waves (3): rendered-DOM assertions\n30\t  (positive + negative) + a real Playwright + Chromium interaction test + a screenshot + John's\n31\t  sign-off before the wave is GREEN. Playwright stays DEV-ONLY (`pytest.importorskip`), never\n32\t  imported by product code.\n33\t- **Spikes gate, they don't block planning:** the 8-day durable-refresh spike gates Wave 4\n34\t  shipping; the Graph-recurrence enumeration spike gates the Wave 5 estimate (run it first).\n35\t- **Baseline:** the current suite is GREEN (1232). Each wave holds or grows it.\n36\t\n37\t---\n38\t\n39\t## Wave 1 â€” Event store + `[calendar]` extra foundation\n40\t\n41\t**Goal.** A faithful on-disk calendar event store and the declared optional dependency surface â€”\n42\tthe substrate every later wave reads/writes â€” with the stdlib invariant provably intact.\n43\t\n44\t**Changes.**\n45\t- `paths.calendar_dir()` â†’ `data_dir()/.anchor/calendar/` (+ per-account subdirs); `.anchor/`\n46\t  already excluded from every distro build.\n47\t- New `calendar_store.py` (repo root, first-party): write/read an event series as RFC-5545\n48\t  `.ics` at `<account>/events/<icalUID>.ics` (one VEVENT per series; RECURRENCE-ID overrides are\n49\t  sibling VEVENTs sharing the UID, keyed `(iCalUID, original-start)`) + a `meta.json` sidecar\n50\t  retaining provider `id`/`etag`, Google `recurringEventId`, **Graph `seriesMasterId`/`type` +\n51\t  the raw Graph JSON** (lossless source for Graph-only recurrence), colorId, sync tokens.\n52\t  `state.json` projection (the flat, render-only occurrence cache) is written here too.\n53\t- Markdown-deadline â†’ store mapping (Anchor-authored deadlines become Anchor-owned events).\n54\t- `pyproject.toml`: declare `calendar = [\"msal\", \"google-auth\", \"icalendar\", \"ical\"]`.\n55\t- `distro.py`: add the scoped calendar allowlist entry; keep the single `pywinpty` exception.\n56\t\n57\t**Done-when.** A round-trip (write a recurring series with an override â†’ read it back) is byte-\n58\tfaithful incl. the raw-Graph-JSON sidecar; AND `distro.py`'s scan is green AND importing the core\n59\tapp WITHOUT the `[calendar]` extra still succeeds (calendar modules surface `CalendarUnavailable`).\n60\t\n61\t**Given/When/Then.**\n62\t- *Given* a series with an RRULE + one EXDATE + one RECURRENCE-ID override, *When* written then\n63\t  re-read via `calendar_store`, *Then* the `.ics` + sidecar reproduce all three faithfully and the\n64\t  override resolves by `(iCalUID, original-start)` (no ghost/duplicate occurrence).\n65\t- *Given* the `[calendar]` extra is NOT installed, *When* the core app imports + `calendar_store`\n66\t  is imported, *Then* the core import path is stdlib-clean (distro scan green) and the calendar\n67\t  module raises/exposes `CalendarUnavailable`, never an `ImportError` stack trace.\n68\t\n69\t---\n70\t\n71\t## Wave 2 â€” Auth (PKCE + loopback + DPAPI; msal/google-auth wrappers)\n72\t\n73\t**Goal.** A connect-once-per-provider OAuth flow that yields a durable, DPAPI-protected token the\n74\tbackground poller can refresh unattended â€” Production-posture, 7-day-tolerant.\n75\t\n76\t**Changes.**\n77\t- New `calendar_auth.py`: PKCE (S256) Auth-Code flow over thin wrappers on `msal` (Microsoft) +\n78\t  `google-auth`/`google-auth-oauthlib` (Google); installed/desktop client; loopback\n79\t  `http://127.0.0.1:<ephemeral>/callback` (never `localhost`, never 8777); `webbrowser.open()`\n80\t  consent; state-CSRF echo check. Persist the (rotated) refresh token DPAPI-wrapped in\n81\t  `.anchor/calendar/<provider>.json`. Assume PKCE-S256 for Microsoft regardless of its discovery\n82\t  doc (the OBSERVED spike quirk).\n83\t- Token-lifecycle: refresh on use; on `invalid_grant`/token-loss set a persisted\n84\t  `needs_reauth` flag (consumed by the UI in Wave 3) â€” never a silent failure.\n85\t- HTTP routes: `do_GET` += `/api/calendar/connect` (mint verifier, open consent) +\n86\t  `/api/calendar/callback` (capture `?code=&state=`, finish PKCE); `do_POST` (token-authed) +=\n87\t  `/api/calendar/refresh` / `/api/calendar/disconnect`.\n88\t- Reuse the OBSERVED 2026-06-15 spike harness (`run-2026-06-15/spike/pkce_loopback_spike.py`).\n89\t\n90\t**Done-when.** Through the fake-auth seam: connect â†’ token DPAPI-wrapped at rest (ciphertext â‰ \n91\tplaintext) â†’ a simulated refresh round-trips â†’ a simulated `invalid_grant` sets `needs_reauth`\n92\t(no exception escapes to the poller).\n93\t\n94\t**Given/When/Then.**\n95\t- *Given* a completed (faked) consent, *When* the callback finishes PKCE, *Then* a refresh token\n96\t  is stored DPAPI-wrapped and is NOT readable as plaintext on disk.\n97\t- *Given* a stored token the provider has revoked, *When* the poller refreshes, *Then* the cycle\n98\t  sets `needs_reauth` + records a poll-failure timestamp and exits cleanly (Shark finding #3).\n99\t\n100\t---\n101\t\n102\t## Wave 3 â€” PULL pipe + EventCalendar display\n103\t\n104\t**Goal.** See ALL of John's calendars, live, in a real month/week/day view â€” incremental, resync-\n105\tsafe, and free of self-echo.\n106\t\n107\t**Changes.**\n108\t- New `calendar_sync.py` PULL pipe: Google `events.list`+`syncToken` (page to the final\n109\t  `nextSyncToken`; `singleEvents=false`; deletions = `status:cancelled`; `410`â†’full resync) +\n110\t  Graph `GET /me/calendarView/delta` (follow `@odata.nextLink`; persist `@odata.deltaLink`; guard\n111\t  the `skipToken` infinite loop; token-lossâ†’full resync). Normalize into `calendar_store`; expand\n112\t  recurrence for display via `ical` Timeline â†’ `state.json`.\n113\t- **Exclude the Anchor-owned calendar id from the inbound/display set** (Shark finding #1,\n114\t  BLOCKER): Anchor's own events render from local state, never from a pull of its own calendar â€”\n115\t  no double-render.\n116\t- Background `threading.Thread(daemon=True)` poller (mirror `_trigger_session_summary`); render\n117\t  reads `state.json` ONLY. Copy vdirsyncer's empty-replica \"replica went empty â‡’ abort, don't\n118\t  wipe\" guard.\n119\t- UI: vendor **EventCalendar (vkurko, MIT)** into `vendor/event-calendar/` (**ship its LICENSE\n120\t  file**); replace the hand-typed `## Today's Calendar` block with a live, `WRITE_LOCK`-guarded\n121\t  month/week/day view + a visible `needs_reauth` / last-sync banner.\n122\t\n123\t**Done-when.** Through the fake-API seam: an initial pull + an incremental delta render correct\n124\toccurrences (incl. one recurring series) in the view; a `410`/token-loss triggers a clean full\n125\tresync; the Anchor-owned calendar never appears twice; a `needs_reauth` flag shows the re-auth\n126\tbanner. UI verification pack passes + John signs off.\n127\t\n128\t**Given/When/Then.**\n129\t- *Given* the Anchor-owned calendar exists and holds a pushed event, *When* the pull pipe runs,\n130\t  *Then* that event renders exactly once (from local state), never duplicated by an inbound pull.\n131\t- *Given* a recurring series with an override from the fake API, *When* pulled + expanded, *Then*\n132\t  the view shows the correct occurrences with the override applied and no ghost instance.\n133\t- *Given* a `410 GONE`, *When* the next pull runs, *Then* the local mirror is rebuilt by full\n134\t  resync without losing the Anchor-owned events (empty-replica guard holds).\n135\t\n136\t---\n137\t\n138\t## Wave 4 â€” PUSH pipe to the dedicated Anchor-owned calendar\n139\t\n140\t**Goal.** Push John's Anchor-authored events OUT to a calendar Anchor owns in each provider â€”\n141\tidempotent, echo-free, and structurally incapable of touching a human event.\n142\t\n143\t> **GATE:** ship only after the 8-day durable-refresh spike confirms the Production token survives\n144\t> (`run-2026-06-15/spike/RUNBOOK.md` step 5). The pipe can be BUILT + stub-tested before the spike\n145\t> resolves; it is not enabled against a real account until the spike is green.\n146\t\n147\t**Changes.**\n148\t- `calendar_sync.py` PUSH pipe: ensure-exists the dedicated **\"Anchor\"** calendar per provider\n149\t  (create if absent; persist its id). Upsert Anchor-owned events by `iCalUID`\n150\t  (Google `events.insert/patch`; Graph `POST/PATCH /me/calendars/<anchorId>/events` with\n151\t  `transactionId` for idempotent create). Optimistic concurrency via ETag/`If-Match` (`412`â†’\n152\t  refetch). Echo-suppress: stamp a self-marker + record the returned ETag; the next inbound delta\n153\t  carrying our marker+etag is dropped.\n154\t- **Hard safety guard:** the push client asserts the target calendar id == the stored Anchor-owned\n155\t  id and REFUSES any other id (falsifier a) â€” tested negatively.\n156\t\n157\t**Done-when.** Through the fake-API seam: an Anchor event upserts into the Anchor-owned calendar\n158\t(idempotent on re-run â€” no duplicate), the echo-suppressor drops the round-tripped delta, AND an\n159\tattempt to push to a non-Anchor calendar id is refused.\n160\t\n161\t**Given/When/Then.**\n162\t- *Given* an Anchor-authored event, *When* push runs twice, *Then* exactly one remote event exists\n163\t  (idempotent by `iCalUID` + `transactionId`).\n164\t- *Given* a pushed event that returns in the next pull delta with our self-marker, *When* the pull\n165\t  processes it, *Then* it is echo-suppressed (no duplicate, no fight with local state).\n166\t- *Given* any calendar id â‰  the stored Anchor-owned id, *When* a write is attempted, *Then* the\n167\t  push client refuses (safety rail).\n168\t\n169\t---\n170\t\n171\t## Wave 5 â€” Recurrence hardening\n172\t\n173\t**Goal.** Make the Graph `recurrencePattern` â†” RRULE boundary correct-or-honest â€” clean RRULE\n174\twhere possible, explicit sidecar-only fallback where Graph is lossy.\n175\t\n176\t> **GATE:** run the 1-day Graph-recurrence enumeration spike FIRST; its lossy-cell count sizes\n177\t> this wave. The fixture table is the test corpus.\n178\t\n179\t**Changes.**\n180\t- Enumerate every Graph `recurrencePattern` variant (daily / weekly / absoluteMonthly /\n181\t  relativeMonthly / absoluteYearly / relativeYearly Ã— single & multiple `daysOfWeek` Ã— `index`\n182\t  first/second/third/fourth/last) into `tests/fixtures/graph_recurrence/`. For each: assert a\n183\t  clean RRULE round-trip OR flag it **sidecar-only, not RRULE-expressible** and render from the\n184\t  retained raw Graph JSON.\n185\t- Override identity `(iCalUID, original-start)` correctness across both providers; never rewrite a\n186\t  series `DTSTART`.\n187\t\n188\t**Done-when.** Every fixture variant either round-trips RRULE cleanly OR is explicitly served from\n189\tthe sidecar (no silent wrong occurrence); the lossy-cell set is documented; override/cancellation\n190\tinstances render correctly with no ghosts/duplicates.\n191\t\n192\t**Given/When/Then.**\n193\t- *Given* a `relativeMonthly` pattern with multiple `daysOfWeek` (the known lossy cell), *When*\n194\t  expanded for display, *Then* occurrences come from the raw-JSON sidecar path and match Graph's\n195\t  \"first day that satisfies\" semantics â€” not a wrong RRULE guess.\n196\t\n197\t---\n198\t\n199\t## Wave 6 â€” Ship: CLI mirror + healthcheck + distro + docs (PROJECT DONE)\n200\t\n201\t**Goal.** Make the surface inspectable, self-tested, distributable, and documented.\n202\t\n203\t**Changes.**\n204\t- `anchor.py` read-only mirror: `cal status` (linked providers, last-sync, `needs_reauth`,\n205\t  counts) + `cal pull` (one foreground incremental pull) â€” honest-absent when unconfigured.\n206\t- `anchor_healthcheck.py` += `check_calendar_surface`, **fully stubbed** (fake-API seam + temp\n207\t  `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR` + no DPAPI key material): walk connect (faked) â†’ DPAPI round-trip â†’ store\n208\t  round-trip â†’ PULL+expand â†’ exclude-own-calendar â†’ PUSH upsert+echo-suppress â†’ safety-rail\n209\t  refusal â†’ restore env/teardown. Never live Google/MS; never binds `:8777`.\n210\t- `distro.py` scan stays green (scoped `[calendar]` allowlist only; Playwright never in product\n211\t  code). Update `CLAUDE.md` (the calendar surface + the `[calendar]` extra + the safety rail).\n212\t\n213\t**Done-when.** `cal status`/`cal pull` mirror the live data read-only; `check_calendar_surface`\n214\truns fully stubbed and GREEN inside the existing healthcheck; `distro.py` scan green; `CLAUDE.md`\n215\tdocuments the surface. Full suite GREEN (â‰¥ baseline).\n216\t\n217\t**Given/When/Then.**\n218\t- *Given* a stubbed project with a connected (faked) provider, *When* `check_calendar_surface`\n219\t  runs, *Then* it walks the full connectâ†’storeâ†’pullâ†’pushâ†’safety-rail path, touches no real\n220\t  network and no `:8777`, and restores all env + temp dirs.\n221\t\n222\t---\n223\t\n224\t## Project DONE\n225\t\n226\tThe project is DONE when **Wave 6** is GREEN: all six waves' acceptance criteria met, the full\n227\tpytest suite green at or above baseline, `distro.py` clean, and `CLAUDE.md` updated. The 8-day\n228\tdurable-refresh spike must be green before Wave 4 is enabled against a real account (it does not\n229\tblock the build/merge of the stubbed pipe).\n230\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e78d70e-5840-44b3-bad2-ee6581f68d36","uuid":"db01bd8a-c463-4edc-8ac1-6af08740b903","timestamp":"2026-06-21T05:00:00.328Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Anchor\\planning\\calendar-v1\\IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md","content":"# Anchor Calendar v1 â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n\n> Crucible Stage 2 output, locked 2026-06-20. Frozen design: `MASTER-PLAN.md`.\n> Build cwd = repo root `C:\\dev\\Anchor`. Suggested branch: `foreman/calendar-v1` (off master).\n> North Star + falsifiers are in `MASTER-PLAN.md Â§1` â€” every wave serves them.\n\ntest-command: python -m pytest -q\n\n## Conventions (read before any wave)\n\n- **No live Google / Microsoft, ever, in any test or healthcheck.** All HTTP goes through a\n  fake-responder seam (monkeypatch the `urllib`/client transport â†’ `tests/fake_calendar_api.py`).\n  No real OAuth dance, no real network, no real DPAPI key material in CI logic.\n- **The `[calendar]` extra is opt-in + lazy + degrading.** `msal`, `google-auth`, `icalendar`,\n  `allenporter/ical` (PyPI `ical`) are imported LAZILY inside the calendar modules only, exactly\n  like `pywinpty` in `pty_manager.py`. With the extra absent, `import`-ing the calendar modules\n  must succeed and surface a `CalendarUnavailable` (\"calendar unavailable\"), never a stack trace.\n  `distro.py`'s import scan gets a NEW scoped allowlist entry for the calendar module(s) only;\n  the core import path must stay stdlib-clean WITHOUT the extra (asserted in Wave 1).\n- **Safety rail (falsifier a):** Anchor only ever issues create/update/delete against the\n  dedicated Anchor-owned calendar it creates per provider. It NEVER holds a write/delete handle\n  on any other calendar. Enforced in code (the push client refuses a non-Anchor calendar id) and\n  tested negatively.\n- **Render reads cache only (falsifier e):** the dashboard/calendar view reads\n  `.anchor/calendar/state.json`; it never makes a sync network call on render.\n- **Token storage:** DPAPI user-scope via `ctypes` `CryptProtectData` (service runs as `.\\john`).\n  The token store tolerates 7-day expiry / `invalid_grant` by surfacing a re-auth state, never a\n  silent stop (Shark finding #3).\n- **UI verification (the v4 lesson)** for UI-changing waves (3): rendered-DOM assertions\n  (positive + negative) + a real Playwright + Chromium interaction test + a screenshot + John's\n  sign-off before the wave is GREEN. Playwright stays DEV-ONLY (`pytest.importorskip`), never\n  imported by product code.\n- **Spikes gate, they don't block planning:** the 8-day durable-refresh spike gates Wave 4\n  shipping; the Graph-recurrence enumeration spike gates the Wave 5 estimate (run it first).\n- **Baseline:** the current suite is GREEN (1232). Each wave holds or grows it.\n\n---\n\n## Wave 1 â€” Event store + `[calendar]` extra foundation\n\n**Goal.** A faithful on-disk calendar event store and the declared optional dependency surface â€”\nthe substrate every later wave reads/writes â€” with the stdlib invariant provably intact.\n\n**Changes.**\n- `paths.calendar_dir()` â†’ `data_dir()/.anchor/calendar/` (+ per-account subdirs); `.anchor/`\n  already excluded from every distro build.\n- New `calendar_store.py` (repo root, first-party): write/read an event series as RFC-5545\n  `.ics` at `<account>/events/<icalUID>.ics` (one VEVENT per series; RECURRENCE-ID overrides are\n  sibling VEVENTs sharing the UID, keyed `(iCalUID, original-start)`) + a `meta.json` sidecar\n  retaining provider `id`/`etag`, Google `recurringEventId`, **Graph `seriesMasterId`/`type` +\n  the raw Graph JSON** (lossless source for Graph-only recurrence), colorId, sync tokens.\n  `state.json` projection (the flat, render-only occurrence cache) is written here too.\n- Markdown-deadline â†’ store mapping (Anchor-authored deadlines become Anchor-owned events).\n- `pyproject.toml`: declare `calendar = [\"msal\", \"google-auth\", \"icalendar\", \"ical\"]`.\n- `distro.py`: add the scoped calendar allowlist entry; keep the single `pywinpty` exception.\n\n**Done-when.** A round-trip (write a recurring series with an override â†’ read it back) is byte-\nfaithful incl. the raw-Graph-JSON sidecar; AND `distro.py`'s scan is green AND importing the core\napp WITHOUT the `[calendar]` extra still succeeds (calendar modules surface `CalendarUnavailable`).\n\n**Given/When/Then.**\n- *Given* a series with an RRULE + one EXDATE + one RECURRENCE-ID override, *When* written then\n  re-read via `calendar_store`, *Then* the `.ics` + sidecar reproduce all three faithfully and the\n  override resolves by `(iCalUID, original-start)` (no ghost/duplicate occurrence).\n- *Given* the `[calendar]` extra is NOT installed, *When* the core app imports + `calendar_store`\n  is imported, *Then* the core import path is stdlib-clean (distro scan green) and the calendar\n  module raises/exposes `CalendarUnavailable`, never an `ImportError` stack trace.\n\n---\n\n## Wave 2 â€” Auth (PKCE + loopback + DPAPI; msal/google-auth wrappers)\n\n**Goal.** A connect-once-per-provider OAuth flow that yields a durable, DPAPI-protected token the\nbackground poller can refresh unattended â€” Production-posture, 7-day-tolerant.\n\n**Changes.**\n- New `calendar_auth.py`: PKCE (S256) Auth-Code flow over thin wrappers on `msal` (Microsoft) +\n  `google-auth`/`google-auth-oauthlib` (Google); installed/desktop client; loopback\n  `http://127.0.0.1:<ephemeral>/callback` (never `localhost`, never 8777); `webbrowser.open()`\n  consent; state-CSRF echo check. Persist the (rotated) refresh token DPAPI-wrapped in\n  `.anchor/calendar/<provider>.json`. Assume PKCE-S256 for Microsoft regardless of its discovery\n  doc (the OBSERVED spike quirk).\n- Token-lifecycle: refresh on use; on `invalid_grant`/token-loss set a persisted\n  `needs_reauth` flag (consumed by the UI in Wave 3) â€” never a silent failure.\n- HTTP routes: `do_GET` += `/api/calendar/connect` (mint verifier, open consent) +\n  `/api/calendar/callback` (capture `?code=&state=`, finish PKCE); `do_POST` (token-authed) +=\n  `/api/calendar/refresh` / `/api/calendar/disconnect`.\n- Reuse the OBSERVED 2026-06-15 spike harness (`run-2026-06-15/spike/pkce_loopback_spike.py`).\n\n**Done-when.** Through the fake-auth seam: connect â†’ token DPAPI-wrapped at rest (ciphertext â‰ \nplaintext) â†’ a simulated refresh round-trips â†’ a simulated `invalid_grant` sets `needs_reauth`\n(no exception escapes to the poller).\n\n**Given/When/Then.**\n- *Given* a completed (faked) consent, *When* the callback finishes PKCE, *Then* a refresh token\n  is stored DPAPI-wrapped and is NOT readable as plaintext on disk.\n- *Given* a stored token the provider has revoked, *When* the poller refreshes, *Then* the cycle\n  sets `needs_reauth` + records a poll-failure timestamp and exits cleanly (Shark finding #3).\n\n---\n\n## Wave 3 â€” PULL pipe + EventCalendar display\n\n**Goal.** See ALL of John's calendars, live, in a real month/week/day view â€” incremental, resync-\nsafe, and free of self-echo.\n\n**Changes.**\n- New `calendar_sync.py` PULL pipe: Google `events.list`+`syncToken` (page to the final\n  `nextSyncToken`; `singleEvents=false`; deletions = `status:cancelled`; `410`â†’full resync) +\n  Graph `GET /me/calendarView/delta` (follow `@odata.nextLink`; persist `@odata.deltaLink`; guard\n  the `skipToken` infinite loop; token-lossâ†’full resync). Normalize into `calendar_store`; expand\n  recurrence for display via `ical` Timeline â†’ `state.json`.\n- **Exclude the Anchor-owned calendar id from the inbound/display set** (Shark finding #1,\n  BLOCKER): Anchor's own events render from local state, never from a pull of its own calendar â€”\n  no double-render.\n- Background `threading.Thread(daemon=True)` poller (mirror `_trigger_session_summary`); render\n  reads `state.json` ONLY. Copy vdirsyncer's empty-replica \"replica went empty â‡’ abort, don't\n  wipe\" guard.\n- UI: vendor **EventCalendar (vkurko, MIT)** into `vendor/event-calendar/` (**ship its LICENSE\n  file**); replace the hand-typed `## Today's Calendar` block with a live, `WRITE_LOCK`-guarded\n  month/week/day view + a visible `needs_reauth` / last-sync banner.\n\n**Done-when.** Through the fake-API seam: an initial pull + an incremental delta render correct\noccurrences (incl. one recurring series) in the view; a `410`/token-loss triggers a clean full\nresync; the Anchor-owned calendar never appears twice; a `needs_reauth` flag shows the re-auth\nbanner. UI verification pack passes + John signs off.\n\n**Given/When/Then.**\n- *Given* the Anchor-owned calendar exists and holds a pushed event, *When* the pull pipe runs,\n  *Then* that event renders exactly once (from local state), never duplicated by an inbound pull.\n- *Given* a recurring series with an override from the fake API, *When* pulled + expanded, *Then*\n  the view shows the correct occurrences with the override applied and no ghost instance.\n- *Given* a `410 GONE`, *When* the next pull runs, *Then* the local mirror is rebuilt by full\n  resync without losing the Anchor-owned events (empty-replica guard holds).\n\n---\n\n## Wave 4 â€” PUSH pipe to the dedicated Anchor-owned calendar\n\n**Goal.** Push John's Anchor-authored events OUT to a calendar Anchor owns in each provider â€”\nidempotent, echo-free, and structurally incapable of touching a human event.\n\n> **GATE:** ship only after the 8-day durable-refresh spike confirms the Production token survives\n> (`run-2026-06-15/spike/RUNBOOK.md` step 5). The pipe can be BUILT + stub-tested before the spike\n> resolves; it is not enabled against a real account until the spike is green.\n\n**Changes.**\n- `calendar_sync.py` PUSH pipe: ensure-exists the dedicated **\"Anchor\"** calendar per provider\n  (create if absent; persist its id). Upsert Anchor-owned events by `iCalUID`\n  (Google `events.insert/patch`; Graph `POST/PATCH /me/calendars/<anchorId>/events` with\n  `transactionId` for idempotent create). Optimistic concurrency via ETag/`If-Match` (`412`â†’\n  refetch). Echo-suppress: stamp a self-marker + record the returned ETag; the next inbound delta\n  carrying our marker+etag is dropped.\n- **Hard safety guard:** the push client asserts the target calendar id == the stored Anchor-owned\n  id and REFUSES any other id (falsifier a) â€” tested negatively.\n\n**Done-when.** Through the fake-API seam: an Anchor event upserts into the Anchor-owned calendar\n(idempotent on re-run â€” no duplicate), the echo-suppressor drops the round-tripped delta, AND an\nattempt to push to a non-Anchor calendar id is refused.\n\n**Given/When/Then.**\n- *Given* an Anchor-authored event, *When* push runs twice, *Then* exactly one remote event exists\n  (idempotent by `iCalUID` + `transactionId`).\n- *Given* a pushed event that returns in the next pull delta with our self-marker, *When* the pull\n  processes it, *Then* it is echo-suppressed (no duplicate, no fight with local state).\n- *Given* any calendar id â‰  the stored Anchor-owned id, *When* a write is attempted, *Then* the\n  push client refuses (safety rail).\n\n---\n\n## Wave 5 â€” Recurrence hardening\n\n**Goal.** Make the Graph `recurrencePattern` â†” RRULE boundary correct-or-honest â€” clean RRULE\nwhere possible, explicit sidecar-only fallback where Graph is lossy.\n\n> **GATE:** run the 1-day Graph-recurrence enumeration spike FIRST; its lossy-cell count sizes\n> this wave. The fixture table is the test corpus.\n\n**Changes.**\n- Enumerate every Graph `recurrencePattern` variant (daily / weekly / absoluteMonthly /\n  relativeMonthly / absoluteYearly / relativeYearly Ã— single & multiple `daysOfWeek` Ã— `index`\n  first/second/third/fourth/last) into `tests/fixtures/graph_recurrence/`. For each: assert a\n  clean RRULE round-trip OR flag it **sidecar-only, not RRULE-expressible** and render from the\n  retained raw Graph JSON.\n- Override identity `(iCalUID, original-start)` correctness across both providers; never rewrite a\n  series `DTSTART`.\n\n**Done-when.** Every fixture variant either round-trips RRULE cleanly OR is explicitly served from\nthe sidecar (no silent wrong occurrence); the lossy-cell set is documented; override/cancellation\ninstances render correctly with no ghosts/duplicates.\n\n**Given/When/Then.**\n- *Given* a `relativeMonthly` pattern with multiple `daysOfWeek` (the known lossy cell), *When*\n  expanded for display, *Then* occurrences come from the raw-JSON sidecar path and match Graph's\n  \"first day that satisfies\" semantics â€” not a wrong RRULE guess.\n\n---\n\n## Wave 6 â€” Ship: CLI mirror + healthcheck + distro + docs (PROJECT DONE)\n\n**Goal.** Make the surface inspectable, self-tested, distributable, and documented.\n\n**Changes.**\n- `anchor.py` read-only mirror: `cal status` (linked providers, last-sync, `needs_reauth`,\n  counts) + `cal pull` (one foreground incremental pull) â€” honest-absent when unconfigured.\n- `anchor_healthcheck.py` += `check_calendar_surface`, **fully stubbed** (fake-API seam + temp\n  `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR` + no DPAPI key material): walk connect (faked) â†’ DPAPI round-trip â†’ store\n  round-trip â†’ PULL+expand â†’ exclude-own-calendar â†’ PUSH upsert+echo-suppress â†’ safety-rail\n  refusal â†’ restore env/teardown. Never live Google/MS; never binds `:8777`.\n- `distro.py` scan stays green (scoped `[calendar]` allowlist only; Playwright never in product\n  code). Update `CLAUDE.md` (the calendar surface + the `[calendar]` extra + the safety rail).\n\n**Done-when.** `cal status`/`cal pull` mirror the live data read-only; `check_calendar_surface`\nruns fully stubbed and GREEN inside the existing healthcheck; `distro.py` scan green; `CLAUDE.md`\ndocuments the surface. Full suite GREEN (â‰¥ baseline).\n\n**Given/When/Then.**\n- *Given* a stubbed project with a connected (faked) provider, *When* `check_calendar_surface`\n  runs, *Then* it walks the full connectâ†’storeâ†’pullâ†’pushâ†’safety-rail path, touches no real\n  network and no `:8777`, and restores all env + temp dirs.\n\n---\n\n## Project DONE\n\nThe project is DONE when **Wave 6** is GREEN: all six waves' acceptance criteria met, the full\npytest suite green at or above baseline, `distro.py` clean, and `CLAUDE.md` updated. The 8-day\ndurable-refresh spike must be green before Wave 4 is enabled against a real account (it does not\nblock the build/merge of the stubbed pipe).\n","numLines":230,"startLine":1,"totalLines":230}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01L6mr3ohESXMoNTNYoaVKn8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Anchor Calendar v1 â€” Planning Trio Summary\n\n**Goal & North Star (LOCKED 2026-06-20)**\n- Build a v1 calendar that **displays all of John's Google + Outlook/M365 calendars** in a real month/week/day view and **pushes John's Anchor-owned events to a dedicated Anchor-owned calendar** in each provider â€” fully local/private, no cloud, no inbound network surface.\n- The hard invariant: Anchor can **NEVER corrupt, delete, or duplicate a human-created event**. Five falsifiers gate the objective: (a) any write to a non-Anchor event, (b) any inbound/webhook surface, (c) silent loss/duplication, (d) a calendar dep breaking `distro.py`'s stdlib scan outside the `[calendar]` extra, (e) a render path making a synchronous network call.\n\n**Locked architecture (from research, not re-litigated)**\n- **Poll, never webhook** â€” background daemon thread; render reads cached `.anchor/calendar/state.json` only, never a sync network call.\n- **Two native REST clients:** Google Calendar v3 (`events.list` + `syncToken`, `410`â†’full resync) + Microsoft Graph (`GET /me/calendarView/delta`, GA v1.0 not beta; guard the `skipToken` loop). Recurring series pulled **un-expanded** (`singleEvents=false`).\n- **Auth:** OAuth2 Auth-Code + PKCE (S256), loopback `127.0.0.1:<ephemeral>` (never `localhost`/8777), DPAPI user-scope token storage via `ctypes` (service runs as `.\\john`).\n\n**Locked decisions**\n- **(A)** OAuth ships as an opt-in `[calendar]` pip-extra (`msal` + `google-auth`), lazy/degrading like `[terminal]=pywinpty`, DPAPI-wrapped at rest.\n- **(B)** Sync scope = **two one-way pipes** (push Anchor-owned out; pull all others read-only). Symmetric merge **deferred** behind a dual-writer tripwire (Â§8).\n- **(C1)** Recurrence expander = `allenporter/ical` accepted inside the extra (adds a compiled pydantic wheel, opt-in only â€” avoids a hand-rolled, silent-failure-prone engine).\n- **(C2)** Google OAuth = design for **Production** posture, but build the token store to **tolerate 7-day expiry**; the 8-day durable-refresh spike confirms before write-back ships.\n- **UI** = vendored **EventCalendar (vkurko, MIT)**, ship its LICENSE; FullCalendar **v6** named fallback. Widget renders **pre-expanded** occurrences â€” the backend owns 100% of recurrence correctness.\n- **Event store** = RFC-5545 `.ics`-per-series + `meta.json` sidecar; sidecar **must retain raw Graph JSON** (Graph relative-monthly/yearly with multiple `daysOfWeek` has no clean RRULE form).\n\n**Premortem mitigations baked into the plan**\n- **Echo display** (Shark BLOCKER #1): the pull pipe **excludes the Anchor-owned calendar id** from inbound â€” Anchor's own events render only from local state.\n- **Silent sync death** (Shark #3): the daemon detects `invalid_grant`/token-loss and surfaces an explicit **\"Calendar needs re-auth\"** state â€” never a silent stop.\n- **Sync engine** references vdirsyncer's **empty-replica abort guard** (\"a replica went empty â‡’ abort, don't propagate deletes\").\n\n**Phased build (6 waves, dependency-forced: store â†’ auth â†’ pull+display â†’ push â†’ harden â†’ ship)**\n- **W1 â€” Event store + `[calendar]` extra:** `calendar_store.py` (ICS + sidecar), `paths.calendar_dir()`, declare the extra + `distro.py` allowlist; assert core import stays stdlib-clean **without** the extra.\n- **W2 â€” Auth:** `calendar_auth.py` PKCE/loopback/DPAPI wrappers over `msal`/`google-auth`; `invalid_grant`â†’`needs_reauth`; connect/callback/refresh/disconnect routes.\n- **W3 â€” PULL + display (UI wave):** `calendar_sync.py` both providers incremental + resync-safe, exclude-own-calendar, EventCalendar widget replacing the hand-typed calendar block.\n- **W4 â€” PUSH pipe** to the dedicated Anchor calendar: upsert by `iCalUID`, echo-suppress, Graph `transactionId`; **hard safety guard refuses any non-Anchor calendar id**. **Gated on the 8-day durable-refresh spike** (build/stub-test now, enable against a real account only after green).\n- **W5 â€” Recurrence hardening:** enumerate every Graph `recurrencePattern` variant into a fixture table; clean RRULE where possible, explicit sidecar-only fallback for lossy cells. **Gated on the 1-day enumeration spike** (run first â€” it sizes the wave).\n- **W6 â€” Ship (PROJECT DONE):** `anchor.py` `cal status`/`cal pull` read-mirror, fully-stubbed `check_calendar_surface` healthcheck (never live Google/MS), distro green, CLAUDE.md.\n\n**Verification standard**\n- Every wave: a **fully-stubbed** healthcheck slice via a fake-HTTP-responder seam â€” never live Google/MS, never binds `:8777`. UI waves add DOM assertions + Playwright/Chromium + screenshot + John's sign-off (the v4 lesson). Playwright stays DEV-ONLY; `distro.py` import scan stays green.\n\n**Shark-Tank record (Stage 1, converged dry)**\n- #1 echo-double-render (BLOCKER, 2 agree) â†’ resolved via exclude-own-calendar. #2 \"is the richer ICS store still needed post-merge-deferral?\" â†’ kept + re-justified (markdown can't hold RRULE/EXDATE/VTIMEZONE). #3 silent sync death â†’ resolved via surfaced re-auth state. Second round produced no new finding.\n\n**Status:** Master Plan + Implementation Plan both locked 2026-06-20; Foreman-ready on suggested branch `foreman/calendar-v1` (off master), baseline suite GREEN (1232).\n\nOne open spike dependency worth tracking: the **8-day durable-refresh spike** gates Wave 4 being enabled against a real account. Want me to `/schedule` a check-in on that spike once you've kicked it off (it needs your Google app registration + 8 days wall-clock per `run-2026-06-15/spike/RUNBOOK.md`)?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":638,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11404,"cache_read_input_tokens":88911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11404},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e78d70e-5840-44b3-bad2-ee6581f68d36","uuid":"765db7ee-c0aa-4ad8-b887-5fce36b6fbb7","request_id":"req_011CcFpFc7zNHi5P5TnpSQBV"}
